# create-jin-app

This repository is a reusable starter kit. Preserve generic, copy-pasteable functionality. Do not add project-specific business logic, hardcoded domain roles, or extra frameworks unless the current app's requirements demand it.

## Tech stack

Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, pnpm.

Backend: Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Firebase Storage, Cloud Functions (Node.js + Firebase Admin SDK).

Do not add Supabase, Drizzle, Hono, tRPC, or a custom HTTP API server. Data lives in Firestore. Server-side work lives in `cloud-functions/src/`.

## Project structure

```text
.cursor/commands/     # Slash commands: create_brief, plan_feature, code_review
.cursor/rules/        # Project rules (project.mdc + ui-ux.mdc always apply)
src/                  # Frontend only
cloud-functions/src/  # Backend only
public/               # Static assets
seed/app-seed.json    # Emulator seed data
scripts/              # Dev / emulator tooling
docs/features/        # Feature docs; do not commit
```

Frontend source belongs under `src/` (`components/`, `pages/`, `routes/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, `services/`, `types/`). Do not create React components or pages outside `src/`. Shared create/add dialogs use `src/components/Modal.tsx`. UI conventions live in `.cursor/rules/ui-ux.mdc` — feature plans must reference them under Global Constraints / UI-UX and only restating product-specific exceptions.

`public/` holds fonts, assets, icons, images, `favicon.ico`, `robots.txt`, and `sitemap.xml`. Keep application logic out of `public/`.

`cloud-functions/lib/` is generated `tsc` output. Never write business logic there. Edit `cloud-functions/src/` and build.

Install packages with `pnpm add`. Add shadcn components with `npx shadcn@latest add`.

## React

Use functional components. No classes/OOP. Extract reusable hooks instead of duplicating stateful logic. Keep shadcn primitives in `src/components/ui/` and compose app components beside them.

## Routing and roles

Routes live in `src/routes/`. This starter must not hardcode Patient, Clinic, Admin, or any other domain role.

Determine user types from the current project's requirements, then create matching route files. Example only if that app actually has those roles:

```text
src/routes/index.tsx
src/routes/auth.routes.tsx
src/routes/patient.routes.tsx
src/routes/clinic.routes.tsx
src/routes/admin.routes.tsx
```

Keep `auth.routes.tsx` generic. The starter ships `/login` (public, noindex) and `/dashboard` plus `/settings` (authenticated). Put additional public pages in `public.routes.tsx`.

## Authentication and authorization

Default local development uses `src/data/local-auth.json` (any email, default password from that file). This is DEV-only and must not be used in production.

Set `VITE_AUTH_MODE=firebase` to use Firebase Auth. Preserve anonymous sign-in, email/password, Google, and anonymous-account linking unless requirements say otherwise.

`src/lib/auth-context.tsx` owns auth state. `src/services/users.ts` owns the user profile (localStorage in local mode, Firestore `users/{uid}` in Firebase mode).

Authorize on both sides: Firestore/Storage rules and Cloud Functions auth checks. Never trust the client alone. Default: users may read/write only their own `users/{uid}` document.

## Firebase and Cloud Functions

Initialize client SDKs in `src/lib/firebase.ts`. Connect Auth, Firestore, Storage, and Functions emulators when `VITE_USE_FIREBASE_EMULATOR=true`.

Keep these reusable function examples: `cloud-functions/src/example/`, `billingTax.ts`, `dataExport.ts`, `index.ts`. Keep them generic.

Use the Admin SDK only inside Cloud Functions (or emulator seed scripts). Do not ship Admin credentials to the browser.

## Environment variables and secrets

Do not read, print, or commit `.env` files. Do not hardcode secrets. Put secret names in `.env.example` with empty values.

Client env vars must be `VITE_*`. Server secrets (`STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, service accounts) belong in Cloud Functions config / Secret Manager, never in `src/`.

If a new variable is required, tell the human:

```text
File:
Variable:
Purpose:
```

## Firestore and seed data

Do not push schema changes to production. Write rules/index updates in `firestore.rules` and `firestore.indexes.json` for the human to deploy.

Seed through `seed/app-seed.json`. Default: `pnpm seed` against the Firebase Emulator. If `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST` is missing, refuse emulator seed.

Production seed is allowed only when the human explicitly asks to seed production. Then:

1. Warn that this writes to the live Firebase project.
2. Require `ALLOW_PRODUCTION_SEED=true` and a real `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` (not `demo-project`).
3. Give the command `pnpm seed:prod`. Do not run it unless the human also asked you to execute it.
4. Never seed production as a side effect of local setup, tests, or `pnpm dev`.

Start emulators with `scripts/start-emulators-functions.mjs` / `pnpm emulators`.

## Code-change workflow

Inspect existing code and adapt it. Do not blindly rewrite. Do not create duplicate helpers. Do not delete unrelated functionality.

Do not modify `docs/features/` unless explicitly asked. Never commit files from `docs/features/`.

Do not modify production Firebase data unless the human explicitly asks (including production seed).

## Git

Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git add` for a commit, or any other git write. Never update git config. Never skip hooks. Never force-push.

When work is ready to save, **give the human the commands**. Do not execute them.

Split work into **multiple logical commits**, not one commit for all changes. Group by purpose:

- `feat:` new user-facing capability
- `fix:` bug fix
- `refactor:` behavior-preserving restructure
- `chore:` tooling, deps, config
- `docs:` documentation / Cursor rules
- `style:` formatting only

Rules for the suggested series:

1. Each commit is one concern (rules, seed tooling, UI, functions, etc.).
2. Messages explain **why**, present tense, 50–72 character subject.
3. Stage only related files per commit. Show `git add <paths>` then `git commit -m "..."`.
4. Do not include `.env`, `src/lib/firebase-config.json`, `cloud-functions/lib/`, `docs/features/`, or secrets.
5. After the commit commands, give a single `git push` (or `git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream).
6. If the human did not ask to publish, omit `git push` or list it as optional.

Example shape (adapt paths and messages to the actual diff):

```bash
git add .cursor/rules/project.mdc .cursorrules
git commit -m "docs: allow explicit production seed and git command handoff"

git add scripts/seed-emulator.mjs package.json
git commit -m "feat: add opt-in production Firestore seed command"

git push
```

## SEO

Use `src/lib/seo.ts` for title, description, canonical URL, Open Graph, and Twitter/X tags.

Public pages: `index,follow`. Private/authenticated/admin/user-specific pages: `noindex,nofollow`. Keep `public/robots.txt` and `public/sitemap.xml` in sync; sitemap includes public URLs only.

## TypeScript, services, errors

Stay strict. Share types in `src/types/`. Frontend data access goes through `src/services/`, not random Firestore calls in components.

Handle errors with user-visible messages for expected failures and `console.error` (or functions logs) for unexpected ones. Do not swallow errors.

## Security and Stripe

Lock down Firestore and Storage rules by default.

Stripe lives only in Cloud Functions. `stripeWebhook` must verify `Stripe-Signature` with `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` before handling events. Never log raw webhook bodies, secrets, or card data. Never call Stripe with the secret key from the client.

## UI/UX and docs

Match existing shadcn/Tailwind patterns, spacing, and dark-mode tokens. Keep demo pages generic.

Update `README.md` and `docs/PORT_HANDLING.md` when ports, scripts, or architecture change. Prefer short, accurate docs over new markdown files.

## Verification

Before claiming done: check structure and imports, run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint`, grep for broken `@server` / tRPC / Hono imports, confirm no secrets were added, confirm `cloud-functions/lib/` was not hand-edited, and confirm `docs/features/` was not changed. Verify UI in the browser when UI behavior changed.
